+## T07 — Shared issue journey and Fountain navigation cutover
+
+Lead: frontend/product; provider lane supplies bounded comment/issue writes.
+Slices: T07-ISSUE-LIST consumes T04-UI/T06-FOUNTAIN for the shared read-only
+list producer. T07-ISSUE-DETAIL consumes that list for the read-only description,
+conversation and safe Markdown producer. T07-ISSUE-COMPOSITION mounts these
+views and matching optional Factory facts in the shared frame. T07-READ consumes
+that composition and T07-FOUNTAIN-NAVIGATION metadata through the independent
+T07-FOUNTAIN-ISSUE-HOST and T07-FOUNTAIN-ISSUE-ROUTES producer/consumer slices,
+plus T04-UI, T06-FOUNTAIN and T06-CONNECT for the complete connected read journey. T07-EDIT
+additionally requires T07-ISSUE-COMMENT, T07-ISSUE-CREATE, T10-WRITES and
+T11-WRITES. The ordinary comment producer is complete; the new-issue form can
+consume its qualified Fountain host and the completed issue-create bridge
+without waiting for desktop GitHub consent. Files: shared issues/editor/
+Markdown/drafts and native route/template joins. Qualify Fountain in its extension
+and GitHub in desktop first. T10-GATEWAY later qualifies desktop Fountain access;
+the shared screen is not reimplemented for that connection.
+
+- **C:** Issue list/filter/create/detail/edit/comment, labels/assignees/status,
+  timestamps/links and Factory progress using the shared editor and renderer.
+  Persist mutations through the T03 shared journal/application mechanism; prove writes on Fountain
+  first, and bind GitHub writes when T11 is available rather than invent retries.
+- **M/C:** Replace the two existing Factory-status subroutes with the source-map
+  `work/{kind}` patterns. Update header/places, active navigation, request/feed/work
+  links and entry dispatch together. Desktop consumes the same typed targets.
+- **V:** Navigate feed → issue → comment → Factory detail → Back/deep link in both
+  hosts; preserve drafts through account switch/restart and show stale/denied
+  states. Extend existing browser integration files and real native route checks.
+
+Done: normal Soda issue navigation uses shared production views in both hosts;
+core provider issue pages remain accessible explicitly. D5 limits issue-only
+collaborator admission until its host capability is implemented and qualified.
+
+## T08 — Shared PR, diff and review experience
+
+Slices: T08-READ requires T00-DIFF and T07-EDIT; T08-WRITE additionally
+requires T10-WRITES and T11-WRITES. Owner: frontend/product. Files:
+`frontend/factory/pulls/` and shared editor/stories; provider operation endpoints
+remain with the Go adapters. Full submissions consume actual operation slices,
+not an unfinished T10/T11 family or an implicit handoff.
+
+- **C:** PR list/detail/conversation/commits/files; split/unified diff; inline and
+  multiline threads; durable draft review versus submitted review; checks and
+  current merge eligibility. Use exact immutable head/base/anchor identities.
+- **C:** Handle force-push/outdated/dismissed reviews, renamed/deleted/binary/large
+  files, partial diff, permission loss and unavailable guarded operations. Keep
+  provider permission/protection rules authoritative. A renderer is not a review
+  state machine or merger.
+- **V:** Both hosts show the same content/layout and support real comment/review
+  submission, refresh and correction. Verify actual Linux WebKitGTK, keyboard/focus,
+  scroll/draft retention during virtualization and stale-head refusal/readback.
+
+Done: the routine PR review journey stays inside the application in either host;
+an external provider link is optional, not the primary issue/PR experience.
+
+## T09 — Native workspaces, execution and credential custody
+
+Slice: T09-EXECUTION requires T02-ENGINE, T05-LIFECYCLE, T05-CREDENTIALS,
+T06-CONNECT and T12-PLACEMENT. Owner: Rust/native with Go/core consumer. Files:
+`lib/factory-host/`, native custody/provider connections, execution client/provenance
+and the existing consuming HostFactory/BrokerExecution interfaces.
+
+- **M/C:** Reuse portable Git/candidate/receipt/output validators; keep Linux host
+  implementation. Native runtime owns enrolled local roots, isolated run worktrees,
+  process identity/descendants/PTY/deadlines, checkpoint/export and restart receipts.
+  Existing user working changes are never overwritten by preparation or cleanup.
+- **C:** D3 defines trusted same-user execution and the actually enforceable role/
+  credential boundaries. Retain repository/capacity/provider sponsorship gates.
+  Git credential helper/SSH agent, collaboration token and provider CLI account
+  remain different integrations. Never scrape private CLI auth formats.
+- **C:** Reuse provider-tools freshness/discovery and supported provider login;
+  existing runs keep their captured executable. Current repository preference is
+  Muse with Spark 1.3 Contributor mode; qualify that supported path before exposing
+  additional selectable harnesses. No silent provider fallback.
+- **V:** Actual native launch/output/stop/descendant cleanup, token withdrawal,
+  crash/restart, worktree ownership, exact candidate capture, role tool capability
+  and stale receipt rejection. A real finite provider run is necessary for final
+  qualification; a subprocess printing text is not that proof.
+- **C/V:** Join actual executor retirement and unresolved outcomes into the
+  production supervisor's close/Quit/crash/restart path. Complete this before
+  T10-INTAKE/T11-INTAKE can enable unattended dispatch; do not defer native
+  process retirement to the final installed acceptance packet.
+
+Done: Factory executes on the Linux host without appliance/Project container assumptions and
+reports unknown retirement honestly. No claim of appliance isolation without proof.
+
+## T10 — Fountain desktop enrollment, gateway and publication
+
+Slices: T10-COMMENT-SNAPSHOT consumes T03-APP/T06-FOUNTAIN for current human
+conditions and idle native revision. T10-COMMENT-NATIVE consumes those conditions
+for the native conditional comment service and recovery. T10-COMMENT-SDK consumes
+that service for live admitted SDK/callback submit/get/cancel. T10-COMMENT consumes
+the SDK for canonical journal/service/HTTP wiring;
+T10-WRITES consumes comments to complete
+the remaining admitted human operations. T10-GATEWAY consumes those operations plus
+T05-CREDENTIALS and T12-PLACEMENT; it adds supported desktop access, typed reads
+and centrally enforced remote placement. T10-PUBLISH consumes that gateway and
+T09-EXECUTION. T10-INTAKE consumes publication to complete automatic issue-driven
+native work. Owner: Go/Fountain with Rust transfer integration. Files:
+`internal/web/collaboration/`, `fountainclient/`, publisher translations and
+necessary Caddy/setup/placement joins. The gateway is not required to construct
+human-operation adapters or to implement GitHub desktop execution.
+
+- **C:** Resolve D2 with a real supported human login and revocable grant. Source
+  contains PKCE support but the scoped desktop gateway grant is new. Bind account,
+  repository, operation kinds, acting service principals and runtime generation.
+  If a host capability is missing, specify the exact external Fountain change and
+  its authorized owner; do not weaken admission to keep the demo working.
+- **C:** Expose typed bounded reads/operations through HTTPS, with current native
+  permission and grant checks. Retain private SDK execution on the appliance.
+  Scope upload to a pending authorized publication; transfer digest-addressed
+  candidate bundle, validate/stage locally, then call existing conditional Git
+  push/PR publication. A successful upload is not successful publication.
+- **C:** Namespace operation identities and retain lookup/cancel receipts. Enforce
+  placement generation at every new operation; prohibit switching execution host
+  until previous work and uncertain effects are retired/reconciled.
+- **V:** Actual Linux desktop → Soda Forge issue → native execution → bounded upload → PR;
+  lost upload/write reply, revoke grant, changed head/base, old runtime generation,
+  expired login and reconnect. Appliance admissions/secret paths remain private.
+- **C/V:** Route eligible Fountain issue changes to the centrally selected
+  runtime, preserving current accepted-input authority and generation checks.
+  Prove automatic issue-to-native-work-to-PR without duplicate appliance dispatch.
+
+Done: local Linux host execution against Soda Forge preserves its supported remote
+operation guarantees; it does not need a mounted appliance Unix socket.
+
+## T11 — GitHub durable mutations and automatic issue intake
+
+Slices: T11-WRITES requires T03-APP and T06-GITHUB. T11-INTAKE additionally
+requires T09-EXECUTION and T12-PLACEMENT. Human mutations do not wait for an
+executor, polling or the Fountain gateway. Owner: Go/provider with core policy.
+Files: `internal/github/{mutations,polling,capabilities}.go`, service intake,
+operation/scan cursor storage and necessary schema/grant definitions.
+
+- **C:** Implement journaled issue/comment/branch/PR/review/thread/allowed merge
+  effects using supported APIs. Bound and serialize mutations; reconcile lost
+  responses with exact observations. Never blindly repeat a timed-out creation.
+  Persist sequential graph progress; partial creation remains visible/recoverable.
+- **C:** Resolve D1 before activation. Enroll repository, actual actor, eligible
+  authors/forks, accepted content rule, sponsorship/capacity and limits. Automated
+  authors cannot create new spending authority through their own issues/comments.
+  Recheck current permissions and revisions before each admitted action.
+- **C:** Conditional authenticated polling, bounded pagination/cursors and rate
+  handling; wake/reconnect reconciliation; deduplicate effects/versions and avoid
+  recursive self-triggering. Do not claim complete event history or atomic remote
+  graph/merge guarantees. Unsupported invariants keep the action unavailable.
+- **V:** In a real authorized GitHub fixture repo: eligible issue auto-start,
+  ineligible issue waits, edits invalidate accepted revision, revoked permission
+  stops progress, own PR/comment does not duplicate work, missed poll/restart
+  catches up, uncertain creation produces no blind duplicate. Validate actual
+  platform support before exposing automatic merge as available.
+
+Done: automatic issue-driven workflow runs on GitHub under the selected policy;
+credential login alone never enables unattended execution.
+
+## T12 — External PR adoption and execution placement
+
+Slices: T12-PLACEMENT requires T01-RUNTIME, T03-APP and T06-CONNECT and is a
+producer for execution, not a late consumer of PR UI. T12-GITHUB-PRS requires
+T08-WRITE/T11-INTAKE; T12-FOUNTAIN-PRS requires T08-WRITE/T10-INTAKE. Owner:
+Go/core and each provider adapter. Files: service intake/placement, provider PR
+reconciliation and persisted subject/placement definitions.
+
+- **C:** Model externally opened PR work independently of Factory-created PRs.
+  Detect eligible open/update/review/check changes and admit the configured review
+  or correction action. Bind exact repository/head/base and explicit authority to
+  execute fork code; a right to view or comment does not authorize execution.
+- **C:** Fountain placement has a central repository/runtime/generation record.
+  Qualify the central Fountain record in T10-GATEWAY; implement its neutral
+  placement contract and the local enforcement in T12-PLACEMENT before dispatch.
+  Desktop GitHub first release supports one configured controller per repository;
+  do not represent a local DB lock as a cross-machine lease. Shared safe automatic
+  transfer between independent GitHub installations is a separate coordination
+  requirement, not a hidden extension of this packet.
+- **V:** External PR → review → feedback → correction; new head invalidates old
+  evidence; duplicate/reordered observations; cancel/revoke during work; appliance
+  versus desktop placement switch with unresolved publication. Verify the current
+  intake path's ignored PR behavior has actually been replaced, not merely hidden.
+
+Done: both issue and external PR triggers are implemented and truthfully scoped.
+
+## T13 — Installed connected journeys and permission parity
+
+Slices: T13-FORGE consumes T08-WRITE/T12-FOUNTAIN-PRS and the existing appliance
+build/install path. T13-GITHUB consumes T14-PACKAGE/T12-GITHUB-PRS;
+T13-FOUNTAIN consumes T14-PACKAGE/T12-FOUNTAIN-PRS. Each is a separate real
+journey, so a missing fixture for one provider need not block checking the other.
+Owner: integration; one fixture operator. Extend existing integration/browser
+files; record the actual installed subject and fresh selected inputs.
+
+| Installed configuration | Required complete journey |
+| --- | --- |
+| Fountain extension + appliance execution | Create issue → standing-policy eligibility → work → PR → review → correction, using shared UI |
+| Linux desktop + Fountain + native execution | Connect/enroll → issue → local work → candidate transfer → PR → review/correction → restart/resume |
+| Linux desktop + GitHub + native execution | Connect/enroll → issue → automatic admitted work → PR → external review → correction → offline/wake/restart reconciliation |
+| External PR on each provider | Detect/adopt eligible subject → review/correction/check status without duplicate dispatch |
+
+Check keyboard/accessibility, deep links/history, account changes, missing action
+capabilities, same-number IDs across providers, long discussions/diffs, draft
+preservation and expected window close/Quit behavior. D5 requires a real issue-only
+collaborator fixture if full collaborator parity is claimed. A source fixture or
+cross-build is not evidence of an installed/native path.
+
+Done: actual retained evidence for each supported matrix cell, with failed and
+unavailable cells visible. Credentials/model access must already be authorized
+for those real runs; planning itself does not operate external repositories.
+
+## T14 — Distribution, updates and one-change proof
+
+Slices: T14-PACKAGE consumes T05-LIFECYCLE/T08-WRITE/T09-EXECUTION and produces
+the installable artifact before T13 desktop checks. T14-UPGRADE and T14-PARITY
+consume all three T13 installed results. Owner: integration. Files: existing
+release-assets desktop additions, manifests, notices and relevant owning docs.
+
+- **C:** Package architecture-matching Linux Go/PG/native assets and production Lit
+  output. Later macOS distribution includes signing/notarization when credentials are available.
+  Keep Storybook out of production. Verify installed binary permissions and data
+  paths. Normal installation must not require development toolchains or containers.
+- **C/V:** Upgrade retained app/backend/store without overwriting data or changing
+  an active run's captured provider executable. Missing signing credentials gate
+  signed distribution, not the buildable/reviewable local implementation.
+  Include retained browser drafts and pending-command bytes. Qualify explicit
+  recovery of historical unscoped writing against verified profile/account
+  ownership; preserve newer writing and never automatically submit a command
+  whose original provider/account binding cannot be established.
+- **V:** Make a visible bounded shared feed/issue/review component change, rebuild
+  both consumers and demonstrate the same result in Fountain and desktop. Installed
+  desktop updates receive new bundled UI through app updates, not magic live edits.
+- **M:** Absorb implemented ownership into existing product/trust/API/credential/
+  configuration/development guides. Keep this backlog current and preserve the
+  independent Canlang/Fountain product boundaries.
+
+Done: the user can install and use the supported desktop product, and shared
+changes are proven across hosts. No push/publication/deployment is implied by
+this plan; those operations use the authorization in their implementation task.
+
+## Ownership and completion
+
+Implementation is sequential under the table above. The responsible owners
+remain Go for workflow, network services and PostgreSQL schema; Rust for native
+lifecycle, execution and credentials; TypeScript/Lit for shared presentation.
+Root locks/manifests, native routes and release inventories are updated by the
+current slice's implementer at their necessary integration point. A former lane
+allocation is not authorization for parallel agents or concurrent writers.
+
+The detailed T00–T14 families retain the behavior requirements below their
+headings; the slice table determines the order and which part is being completed.
+Do not mark an entire family complete because one sub-slice passed. Earlier
+process separation and component-workbench checks remain useful evidence at their
+actual scope, not credit for connected desktop execution or new issue/PR screens.
