+An ordinary save without a review is not a result. Missing transitions return
+scoped `none`; this does not prove that consultation stopped or credit was not
+consumed. Unknown/foreign/non-draft input returns private 404; malformed or
+ambiguous records refuse. Queries are rejected, admission is rechecked before
+no-store disclosure, and the read wires no chooser, funding or work. Native
+product routes and the Fountain private proxy expose the same read. The shared
+UI exploration journal remains its explicit consumer.
+
+`Work.Handler` owns recorded issue/journey, assignment and priority-comparison
+reads over `service.Issues` and `service.WorkReads`. Hosts bind canonical actor/
+host and current admission, and supply resource visibility, acceptance status,
+runtime membership and navigation through the existing service ports. Error
+presenters retain sanitized provider failures without importing a session/SDK.
+Mixed store ports refuse. Canonical numeric path IDs, bounded comparison cursors
+and private scope-history query limits keep their existing contracts. Reads
+recheck host admission before response, preserve incomplete/missing facts, and
+create no runtime inventory, model consultation, authority, task or workflow.
+The private request scope-comparison endpoint belongs to `Requests.Handler`
+and retains owner admission and recorded mapping semantics after store reopen.
+
+`Repositories.Handler` owns repository status/access, activity, policy, runtime
+capacity/operator/environment grants, sponsorship and repair-allowance transport.
+Hosts bind the canonical actor/host and a separate nonsecret command principal;
+request bodies cannot choose attribution. Mutations require that principal and
+current admission before persistence. Existing services retain current
+administration, operator, environment and sponsorship custody checks, revision
+CAS and durable repair-command replay. Status/access reads recheck admission
+before response and grant no work. Concrete repository service ports must use
+the selected canonical store; policy/runtime writers remain explicit host ports.
+Visibility/authority and host-specific error presenters preserve sanitized
+refusals without a native session dependency. Missing ports refuse. Commands use
+the shared strict 64 KiB JSON decoder and responses use no-store. Fountain now
+supplies its current ports through this owner; construction starts no listener,
+runtime, model call or background work.
+
+`Runs.Handler` owns recorded run-status and explicit repository/run intervention
+routes. Hosts bind actor/host and a separate command principal, current account/
+channel admission and canonical services over the selected store. Repository
+commands require fresh visibility; services retain current execution authority,
+exact run/repository scope and takeover destination admission. Reads grant no
+execution. Commands recheck host admission after strict bounded JSON decoding,
+and successful reads/commands recheck it before disclosure. A changed account
+cannot select another actor or principal through the request. Missing admission,
+principal or mismatched service stores refuse. Status rejects query parameters.
+Pending/unconfirmed effects, revision/command conflicts and durable retry/context
+outcomes retain their canonical responses; native errors use host presenters.
+The coordinator remains the single workflow/journal owner. Fountain supplies its
+current native ports through the same transport. Construction launches no work,
+listener, process, recovery or model call.
+
+`Output.Serve` owns the read-only WebSocket protocol over an already admitted
+`service.OutputAttachment`. Hosts retain origin/private-channel validation,
+upgrade and peer registration/draining. The attachment binds canonical actor,
+repository, run and runtime incarnation; its immutable `RunID` also constrains
+the handshake before any output read. Hosts must supply current account admission
+and a handshake validator for their repository label and account generation.
+The existing `repository_id`/`session_generation` wire fields are host labels,
+not authority or an implicit canonical mapping; a native host binds its own
+profile generation without fabricating a Fountain session.
+
+The shared protocol retains a five-second/4 KiB strict JSON handshake, bounded
+cursor, text/base64 frames, finite read-failure budget, status suppression,
+heartbeat and terminal-byte drain before EOF. Missing attachment/admission/
+handshake ports refuse. Current admission is checked before and after each
+output read, and the service independently checks current resource access and
+incarnation. Further viewer input closes with policy violation and never reaches
+the source. Host cancellation closes the connection and joins its input reader;
+construction/attachment never launches or resumes an agent or changes its run.
+Fountain consumes this same protocol with native channel and generation ports.
+
+`Records.Handler` owns library search/item/history and verified artifact downloads.
+Hosts bind actor/host and mandatory current account/channel admission; the
+existing `Library` and `Artifacts` services receive explicit source and current
+resource-visibility ports. Library reads retain current/history filters, bounded
+pages, exact revision projections and string repository IDs. Downloads retain
+complete-upload, metadata/size/digest checks and owned verified bytes before
+attachment, sandbox/nosniff/private-no-store and HTTP range handling. The handler
+rechecks host admission before JSON or download headers/bytes. Missing admission
+or service ports refuse. Known hidden/missing records stay private; unknown
+visibility/storage and invalid retained content return sanitized unavailable
+responses. Fountain supplies its native visibility ports through the same owner.
+These reads start no work, upload completion, model call or process; worker MCP
+record contracts remain with their existing owners.
+
+`Acceptances.Handler` owns bounded acceptance previews and explicit admit/
+withdraw commands over the existing service and coordinator journal. Hosts bind
+actor/host, current channel/account admission and visibility/execution ports;
+those authority ports must recheck the bound account as well as repository
+permission after evidence reads and before persistence. Commands use the shared
+strict 64 KiB decoder, and bodies cannot choose the approver. Preview queries
+retain the 8 KiB/50 distinct canonical comment-ID bounds. Reads and commands
+recheck host admission before successful responses. Exact decision replay,
+predecessor conflicts, withdrawal latches and incomplete/unavailable evidence
+retain their canonical outcomes. `AcceptanceDecisionError` also serves work
+readback; there is one refusal renderer, with sanitized host authority errors.
+No preview or construction dispatches work or replaces the journal.
+
+Verification-allowance GET/POST belongs to `Requests.Handler`. Its existing
+service retains private owner checks, current administration, exact repository
+admission, command replay, increasing finite limits, usage and revision CAS.
+POST requires a separate host-supplied `Principal`; bodies cannot select it.
+Queries refuse, commands use bounded strict JSON, and host admission is checked
+after decoding and before successful disclosure. Replays return current limits
+and usage while keeping captured command attribution. These operations launch
+no checks, runtime, work driver or model call.
+
+`Workers.Handler` owns the fixed `/mcp` route, POST-only/browser-Origin rules,
+capability-header and Bearer/HMAC authentication, admitted scope/state/expiry
+checks, generic refusals and bounded request-body handoff. It retains a private
+copy of the persistent key. Missing capability, admission or protocol ports
+refuse; it never treats an active row alone as current runtime admission.
+
+Hosts supply `CapabilitySource`, current `Admit` and `Protocol` functions. Native
+composition can supply `service.WorkerAdmission.Prepare` directly, without an
+appliance API/session, Project inventory or native callback headers. The existing
+Forge adapter composes its current worker/controller admission and role-filtered
+MCP SDK server through those same ports. Per-tool authorization, schemas, rate
+limits, durable work and execution remain with their existing owners.
+
+Protocol construction follows authentication and admission; its capability is
+server-supplied and must retain the authenticated immutable scope. Errors expose
+no source/configuration/credential details. Body limiting bounds what the protocol
+can read; that protocol owns decoding and the response to an oversized body.
+Listener permissions, private socket ownership, credential delivery/rotation,
+process lifetime and installed native qualification belong to host composition.
+
+Worker definitions and payload contracts live in
+[mcpwire](../mcpwire/README.md); the shared role-filtered SDK server and tool
+routing live in [mcpserver](../mcpserver/README.md). Hosts compose those owners
+with their current runtime/service ports.
diff --git a/internal/factory/httpapi/acceptance_errors.go b/internal/factory/httpapi/acceptance_errors.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e5042c0dd8e069afb269694918514d21a21819ac
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/factory/httpapi/acceptance_errors.go
@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@
+package httpapi
+
+import (
+	"errors"
+	"net/http"
+	"net/url"
+	"strconv"
+
+	"github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory"
+	"github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory/control"
+	factoryservice "github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory/service"
+)
+
+func (s Acceptances) applicationError(w http.ResponseWriter, err error) {
+	switch {
+	case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrAcceptanceAccess):
+		s.authorityError(w, err)
+	case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrAcceptanceSource):
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_source", "Selected sources must name an exact native comment revision.")
+	case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrAcceptancePrerequisite):
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_prerequisite", "Prerequisites must name their endpoint repository and issue.")
+	case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrAcceptanceInvalid):
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_acceptance", "Acceptance must name its decision and exact selected revisions.")
+	default:
+		AcceptanceDecisionError(w, err)
+	}
+}
+
+// AcceptanceDecisionError maps acceptance failures to status codes.
+// Refused or changed inputs conflict with 409; unavailable evidence or
+// service reports 503, never a validity verdict.
+func AcceptanceDecisionError(w http.ResponseWriter, err error) {
+	var refusal *control.AcceptanceRefusal
+	switch {
+	case errors.As(err, &refusal):
+		acceptanceRefusalError(w, refusal)
+	default:
+		CommandError(w, err)
+	}
+}
+
+func acceptanceRefusalError(w http.ResponseWriter, refusal *control.AcceptanceRefusal) {
+	body := map[string]any{"error": refusal.Reason, "message": acceptanceRefusalMessage(refusal.Reason)}
+	switch refusal.Reason {
+	case control.RefusalIncompleteEvidence, control.RefusalNativeBusy, control.RefusalSnapshotUnavailable:
+		writeJSON(w, 503, body)
+	default:
+		writeJSON(w, 409, body)
+	}
+}
+
+func acceptanceRefusalMessage(reason string) string {
+	switch reason {
+	case control.RefusalStaleEvidence:
+		return "Native state changed during verification; refresh and retry."
+	case control.RefusalIncompleteEvidence:
+		return "Native evidence is incomplete; nothing was recorded."
+	case control.RefusalNativeBusy:
+		return "Native writers are busy; retry after they settle."
+	case control.RefusalSnapshotUnavailable:
+		return "Native evidence is unavailable; nothing was recorded."
+	case control.RefusalIssueHidden:
+		return "The bound actor cannot see the target issue."
+	case control.RefusalObjectiveChanged:
+		return "The issue title or body changed; accept the new revision."
+	case control.RefusalSourceMissing:
+		return "A selected comment no longer exists; accept the current set."
+	case control.RefusalSourceHidden:
+		return "A selected comment is no longer visible."
+	case control.RefusalSourceChanged:
+		return "A selected comment changed; accept the new revision."
+	case control.RefusalEdgeHidden:
+		return "A prerequisite edge is no longer visible."
+	case control.RefusalEdgeChanged:
+		return "The prerequisite edge set changed; adopt the revised set."
+	case control.RefusalPrereqUnknown:
+		return "The named prerequisite acceptance does not exist."
+	case control.RefusalPrereqStale:
+		return "The prerequisite acceptance moved; adopt the current head."
+	case control.RefusalCreationUnverified:
+		return "Creation provenance is unverified; adopt explicitly."
+	case control.RefusalCreationEdited:
+		return "The issue changed after creation; adopt explicitly."
+	case control.RefusalCreationBlocked:
+		return "The issue has prerequisites; adopt explicitly."
+	case control.RefusalCreationFactory:
+		return "Factory-created issues need explicit human adoption."
+	default:
+		return "Creation needs standing policy and a code-write creator."
+	}
+}
+
+func acceptancePreviewReadError(w http.ResponseWriter, err error) {
+	var refusal *control.AcceptanceRefusal
+	if errors.As(err, &refusal) {
+		acceptanceRefusalError(w, refusal)
+		return
+	}
+	writeError(w, 503, "native_evidence_unavailable", "Current native acceptance evidence is unavailable.")
+}
+
+func parseAcceptancePreviewCommentIDs(raw string) ([]string, bool) {
+	if len(raw) > 8192 {
+		return nil, false
+	}
+	values, err := url.ParseQuery(raw)
+	if err != nil {
+		return nil, false
+	}
+	for key := range values {
+		if key != "comment_id" {
+			return nil, false
+		}
+	}
+	ids := values["comment_id"]
+	if len(ids) > factory.MaxAcceptedSources {
+		return nil, false
+	}
+	seen := make(map[string]struct{}, len(ids))
+	for i, value := range ids {
+		id, ok := positiveID(value)
+		if !ok {
+			return nil, false
+		}
+		canonical := strconv.FormatInt(id, 10)
+		if _, exists := seen[canonical]; exists {
+			return nil, false
+		}
+		seen[canonical] = struct{}{}
+		ids[i] = canonical
+	}
+	return ids, true
+}
diff --git a/internal/factory/httpapi/acceptances.go b/internal/factory/httpapi/acceptances.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b931524efdeee9c2d29bd025f42b85fb8a4ed4cb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/factory/httpapi/acceptances.go
@@ -0,0 +1,153 @@
+package httpapi
+
+import (
+	"errors"
+	"net/http"
+	"strconv"
+
+	"github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/collaboration"
+	factoryservice "github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory/service"
+)
+
+// Acceptances serves manual decisions over the existing admission journal.
+// Hosts bind identity and supply current channel/account, visibility and
+// execution-authority ports. Request bodies never choose the approver.
+type Acceptances struct {
+	Service         factoryservice.Acceptances
+	Host            collaboration.HostID
+	Actor           collaboration.ActorID
+	Visibility      factoryservice.WorkVisibility
+	Current         func(http.ResponseWriter, *http.Request) bool
+	AuthorityError  func(http.ResponseWriter, error)
+	VisibilityError func(http.ResponseWriter, error)
+}
+
+func (s Acceptances) Handler() http.Handler {
+	mux := http.NewServeMux()
+	register := func(method, path string, serve http.HandlerFunc) {
+		mux.HandleFunc(method+" "+path, func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+			if r.Method != method {
+				w.Header().Set("Allow", method)
+				writeError(w, 405, "method_not_allowed", "HTTP method not supported.")
+				return
+			}
+			if s.current(w, r) {
+				serve(w, r)
+			}
+		})
+	}
+	base := "/api/repositories/{repositoryID}/factory/issues/{issueID}"
+	register(http.MethodGet, base+"/acceptance-preview", s.preview)
+	register(http.MethodPost, base+"/acceptances", s.admit)
+	register(http.MethodPost, base+"/withdrawal", s.withdraw)
+	return mux
+}
+
+func (s Acceptances) current(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) bool {
+	return currentAccount(w, r, s.Host, s.Actor, s.Current)
+}
+
+func (s Acceptances) scope(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) (collaboration.RepositoryID, string, bool) {
+	id, valid := positiveID(r.PathValue("repositoryID"))
+	if !valid {
+		writeError(w, 404, "not_found", "Repository not found.")
+		return 0, "", false
+	}
+	repository := collaboration.RepositoryID(id)
+	if s.Visibility == nil {
+		s.visibilityError(w, factoryservice.ErrAcceptanceUnavailable)
+		return 0, "", false
+	}
+	if err := s.Visibility(r.Context(), s.Actor, repository); err != nil {
+		s.visibilityError(w, err)
+		return 0, "", false
+	}
+	index, valid := positiveID(r.PathValue("issueID"))
+	if !valid {
+		writeError(w, 404, "not_found", "Factory issue not found.")
+		return 0, "", false
+	}
+	return repository, strconv.FormatInt(index, 10), true
+}
+
+func (s Acceptances) preview(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+	if r.URL.ForceQuery {
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Malformed acceptance preview query.")
+		return
+	}
+	comments, valid := parseAcceptancePreviewCommentIDs(r.URL.RawQuery)
+	if !valid {
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Use at most 50 distinct positive comment_id values.")
+		return
+	}
+	repository, issue, ok := s.scope(w, r)
+	if !ok {
+		return
+	}
+	view, err := s.Service.Preview(r.Context(), s.Actor, repository, issue, comments)
+	if err != nil {
+		if errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrAcceptanceAccess) {
+			s.authorityError(w, err)
+		} else {
+			acceptancePreviewReadError(w, err)
+		}
+		return
+	}
+	if s.current(w, r) {
+		writeJSON(w, 200, view)
+	}
+}
+
+func (s Acceptances) admit(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+	repository, issue, ok := s.scope(w, r)
+	if !ok {
+		return
+	}
+	var in factoryservice.AcceptanceChange
+	if !decodeObject(w, r, &in) || !s.current(w, r) {
+		return
+	}
+	result, err := s.Service.Admit(r.Context(), s.Actor, repository, issue, in)
+	if err != nil {
+		s.applicationError(w, err)
+		return
+	}
+	if s.current(w, r) {
+		writeJSON(w, 201, result)
+	}
+}
+
+func (s Acceptances) withdraw(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+	repository, issue, ok := s.scope(w, r)
+	if !ok {
+		return
+	}
+	var in factoryservice.AcceptanceWithdrawal
+	if !decodeObject(w, r, &in) || !s.current(w, r) {
+		return
+	}
+	result, err := s.Service.Withdraw(r.Context(), s.Actor, repository, issue, in)
+	if err != nil {
+		s.applicationError(w, err)
+		return
+	}
+	if s.current(w, r) {
+		writeJSON(w, 200, result)
+	}
+}
+
+func (s Acceptances) authorityError(w http.ResponseWriter, err error) {
+	if s.AuthorityError != nil {
+		s.AuthorityError(w, err)
+		return
+	}
+	writeError(w, 503, "authority_unavailable", "Current acceptance authority is unavailable.")
+}
+
+func (s Acceptances) visibilityError(w http.ResponseWriter, err error) {
+	if s.VisibilityError != nil {
+		s.VisibilityError(w, err)
+		return
+	}
+	writeError(w, 503, "authority_unavailable", "Current repository visibility is unavailable.")
+}
diff --git a/internal/factory/httpapi/command_errors.go b/internal/factory/httpapi/command_errors.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7664d4654705bae13367cf8f9b617fee9d4cf440
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/factory/httpapi/command_errors.go
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+package httpapi
+
+import (
+	"errors"
+	"net/http"
+
+	"github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory/control"
+	factoryservice "github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory/service"
+	"github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/store"
+)
+
+// CommandError renders canonical Factory command outcomes for every host.
+func CommandError(w http.ResponseWriter, err error) {
+	switch {
+	case errors.Is(err, store.ErrCommandConflict):
+		writeError(w, 409, "command_conflict", "Command identity reused for different content.")
+	case errors.Is(err, store.ErrStaleRevision):
+		writeError(w, 412, "stale_revision", "Grant changed while applying; refresh and retry.")
+	case errors.Is(err, control.ErrCommandRunning):
+		writeJSON(w, 202, map[string]any{"running": true})
+	case errors.Is(err, control.ErrIneffectiveAuthority):
+		writeError(w, 409, "authority_ineffective", "Current grants do not authorize this action.")
+	default:
+		writeError(w, 503, "store_unavailable", "Factory authority storage is unavailable.")
+	}
+}
+
+// RequestReadError keeps owner-private missing requests undisclosed.
+func RequestReadError(w http.ResponseWriter, err error) {
+	if errors.Is(err, store.ErrNotFound) || errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrRequestNotFound) {
+		writeError(w, http.StatusNotFound, "not_found", "Build request not found.")
+		return
+	}
+	CommandError(w, err)
+}
diff --git a/internal/factory/httpapi/feed.go b/internal/factory/httpapi/feed.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..fc1e4248f05b7448676579356fcc941a6d82409c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/factory/httpapi/feed.go
@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+package httpapi
+
+import (
+	"encoding/json"
+	"net/http"
+	"strings"
+
+	"github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/collaboration"
+	factoryservice "github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory/service"
+)
+
+// Feed serves the shared catalogue, feed and subscription protocol for one
+// host-authenticated principal. Hosts supply current authentication/channel and
+// origin admission; Visibility and Posts retain per-resource authority. No
+// request header, query or body selects Actor or Host.
+type Feed struct {
+	Service    factoryservice.Feed
+	Posts      factoryservice.Posts
+	Commands   factoryservice.PostCommands
+	AuthorName string
+	Host       collaboration.HostID
+	Actor      collaboration.ActorID
+	Visibility factoryservice.RepositoryVisibility
+	// Current must recheck this principal's host admission and render its own
+	// refusal when it returns false. Missing admission always refuses.
+	Current func(http.ResponseWriter, *http.Request) bool
+}
+
+// Handler constructs no listener, session, provider client or work driver.
+// The host mounts it only behind its authenticated browser or private IPC path.
+func (s Feed) Handler() http.Handler {
+	return http.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+		var serve http.HandlerFunc
+		methods := http.MethodGet
+		switch r.URL.Path {
+		case "/api/factory/repositories":
+			serve = s.repositories
+		case "/api/factory/feed":
+			serve = s.page
+		case "/api/factory/feed/subscription":
+			serve = s.subscription
+			methods += ", " + http.MethodPut
+		case "/api/factory/feed/posts":
+			serve, methods = s.submitPost, http.MethodPost
+		default:
+			if rest, ok := strings.CutPrefix(r.URL.Path, "/api/factory/feed/posts/"); ok {
+				id, tail, hasTail := strings.Cut(rest, "/")
+				if id != "" && (!hasTail || tail != "") {
+					switch tail {
+					case "":
+						serve = s.readPost
+					case "replies":
+						serve = s.replies
+					case "retry":
+						serve, methods = s.retryPost, http.MethodPost
+					default:
+						if command, ok := strings.CutPrefix(tail, "retry/"); ok && !strings.Contains(command, "/") {
+							serve = s.retryReceipt
+							r.SetPathValue("command", command)
+						}
+					}
+					r.SetPathValue("id", id)
+				}
+			}
+			if serve == nil {
+				http.NotFound(w, r)
+				return
+			}
+		}
+		if r.Method != methods && !(r.URL.Path == "/api/factory/feed/subscription" && (r.Method == http.MethodGet || r.Method == http.MethodPut)) {
+			w.Header().Set("Allow", methods)
+			writeError(w, 405, "method_not_allowed", "HTTP method not supported.")
+			return
+		}
+		if s.current(w, r) {
+			if strings.HasPrefix(r.URL.Path, "/api/factory/feed/posts") {
+				port := s.Posts.Store
+				if r.Method == http.MethodPost {
+					port = s.Commands.Posts.Store
+				}
+				if port == nil || port != s.Service.Store {
+					writeError(w, 503, "store_unavailable", "Feed post transport is unavailable.")
+					return
+				}
+			}
+			serve(w, r)
+		}
+	})
+}
+
+func (s Feed) current(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) bool {
+	return currentAccount(w, r, s.Host, s.Actor, s.Current)
+}
+
+func currentAccount(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request, host collaboration.HostID, actor collaboration.ActorID, current func(http.ResponseWriter, *http.Request) bool) bool {
+	if actor <= 0 || !collaboration.ValidID(string(host)) || current == nil || r.Context().Err() != nil {
+		writeError(w, 503, "authority_unavailable", "Current Factory account admission is unavailable.")
+		return false
+	}
+	return current(w, r)
+}
+
+func writeJSON(w http.ResponseWriter, status int, value any) {
+	body, err := json.Marshal(value)
+	if err != nil {
+		status = http.StatusInternalServerError
+		body = []byte(`{"error":{"code":"internal_error","message":"Cannot encode response."}}`)
+	}
+	w.Header().Set("Content-Type", "application/json; charset=utf-8")
+	w.Header().Set("Cache-Control", "no-store")
+	w.WriteHeader(status)
+	_, _ = w.Write(append(body, '\n'))
+}
+
+func writeError(w http.ResponseWriter, status int, code, message string) {
+	writeJSON(w, status, map[string]any{"error": map[string]string{"code": code, "message": message}})
+}
diff --git a/internal/factory/httpapi/feed_page.go b/internal/factory/httpapi/feed_page.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..259e2687433f847dbc3b96e8273a0aba8bfe3238
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/factory/httpapi/feed_page.go
@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@
+package httpapi
+
+import (
+	"errors"
+	"net/http"
+	"strconv"
+	"strings"
+
+	"github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory"
+	factoryservice "github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory/service"
+)
+
+// ParseFeedQuery admits one combined feed query from its URL
+// parameters: comma-separated repository scope, optional kinds, a
+// bounded window and the resume cursor.
+func ParseFeedQuery(r *http.Request) (factory.FeedQuery, error) {
+	var query factory.FeedQuery
+	seen := make(map[int64]bool)
+	for _, field := range strings.Split(r.URL.Query().Get("repositories"), ",") {
+		field = strings.TrimSpace(field)
+		if field == "" {
+			continue
+		}
+		repository, err := strconv.ParseInt(field, 10, 64)
+		if err != nil || repository <= 0 {
+			return factory.FeedQuery{}, factoryservice.ErrFeedQueryInvalid
+		}
+		if !seen[repository] {
+			seen[repository] = true
+			query.Repositories = append(query.Repositories, repository)
+		}
+	}
+	if kinds := strings.TrimSpace(r.URL.Query().Get("kinds")); kinds != "" {
+		query.Kinds = strings.Split(kinds, ",")
+		for i, kind := range query.Kinds {
+			query.Kinds[i] = strings.TrimSpace(kind)
+		}
+	}
+	limit := 50
+	if raw := strings.TrimSpace(r.URL.Query().Get("limit")); raw != "" {
+		parsed, err := strconv.Atoi(raw)
+		if err != nil {
+			return factory.FeedQuery{}, factoryservice.ErrFeedQueryInvalid
+		}
+		limit = parsed
+	}
+	query.Limit = limit
+	query.View = strings.TrimSpace(r.URL.Query().Get("view"))
+	query.Search = strings.TrimSpace(r.URL.Query().Get("search"))
+	query.Role = strings.TrimSpace(r.URL.Query().Get("role"))
+	query.Current = r.URL.Query().Get("current") == "true"
+	query.Cursor = strings.TrimSpace(r.URL.Query().Get("cursor"))
+	if err := query.Validate(); err != nil {
+		return factory.FeedQuery{}, err
+	}
+	return query, nil
+}
+
+// page serves the caller's subscribed combined feed window:
+// subscription narrowing, then per-entry visibility recheck. The
+// subscriber is the host-admitted caller, never a body field.
+func (s Feed) page(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+	query, err := ParseFeedQuery(r)
+	if err != nil {
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Combined feed query is invalid.")
+		return
+	}
+	view, err := s.Service.Page(r.Context(), s.Actor, query, r.URL.Query().Get("scope") == "project", s.Visibility, s.Posts)
+	if err != nil {
+		switch {
+		case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrFeedSubscriptionUnavailable):
+			writeError(w, 503, "store_unavailable", "Could not read feed subscription.")
+		case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrFeedProjectScope):
+			writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Select one project.")
+		case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrFeedRepositoryUnavailable):
+			writeError(w, 404, "repository_not_found", "Project is not visible.")
+		default:
+			writeError(w, 503, "store_unavailable", "Could not read combined feed.")
+		}
+		return
+	}
+	if s.current(w, r) {
+		writeJSON(w, 200, view)
+	}
+}
diff --git a/internal/factory/httpapi/feed_posts.go b/internal/factory/httpapi/feed_posts.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..82cf081c1dbf9ae7c10710c70a6b6788b2e98c6d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/factory/httpapi/feed_posts.go
@@ -0,0 +1,180 @@
+package httpapi
+
+import (
+	"encoding/json"
+	"errors"
+	"net/http"
+	"strconv"
+
+	"github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory"
+	factoryservice "github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/factory/service"
+	"github.com/levitateos/sodaos/internal/strictjson"
+)
+
+// parseFeedPostBody admits one comment POST body: scope, bounded
+// text and idempotency key. The author is the host-admitted caller.
+func parseFeedPostBody(data []byte) (factory.PostRequest, error) {
+	var req factory.PostRequest
+	if err := json.Unmarshal(data, &req); err != nil {
+		return factory.PostRequest{}, factoryservice.ErrFeedQueryInvalid
+	}
+	if err := req.Validate(); err != nil {
+		return factory.PostRequest{}, err
+	}
+	return req, nil
+}
+
+// submitPost adapts one admitted durable submission. Only background
+// continuation judges, authors or applies effects.
+func (s Feed) submitPost(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+	if r.Method != http.MethodPost {
+		writeError(w, 405, "invalid_request", "Feed posts use POST only.")
+		return
+	}
+	var raw json.RawMessage
+	if err := strictjson.Decode(http.MaxBytesReader(w, r.Body, 65536), &raw); err != nil {
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Feed post body is invalid.")
+		return
+	}
+	req, err := parseFeedPostBody(raw)
+	if err != nil {
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Feed post body is invalid.")
+		return
+	}
+	if !s.current(w, r) {
+		return
+	}
+	response, err := s.Commands.Submit(r.Context(), s.Actor, s.AuthorName, req)
+	if err != nil {
+		switch {
+		case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostInputInvalid):
+			writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Feed post body is invalid.")
+		case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostVisibility):
+			writeError(w, 404, "repository_not_found", "Repository is not visible.")
+		case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostSourceNotFound):
+			writeError(w, 404, "source_not_found", "The parent post is not visible.")
+		default:
+			writeError(w, 503, "store_unavailable", "Could not save the feed post request.")
+		}
+		return
+	}
+	if s.current(w, r) {
+		writeJSON(w, 200, response)
+	}
+}
+
+// readPost serves stored post/record facts through current
+// visibility. Reads do not fund, judge, draft or apply effects.
+func (s Feed) readPost(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+	if r.Method != http.MethodGet {
+		writeError(w, 405, "invalid_request", "Feed post reads only.")
+		return
+	}
+	view, err := s.Posts.Read(r.Context(), s.Actor, r.PathValue("id"))
+	if err != nil {
+		if errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostNotFound) || errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostVisibility) {
+			writeError(w, 404, "comment_not_found", "Feed post is not found.")
+		} else {
+			writeError(w, 503, "store_unavailable", "Could not read the post request.")
+		}
+		return
+	}
+	if s.current(w, r) {
+		writeJSON(w, 200, view)
+	}
+}
+
+func (s Feed) replies(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+	q := r.URL.Query()
+	repository, err := strconv.ParseInt(q.Get("repository"), 10, 64)
+	if err != nil || repository <= 0 {
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Choose a project.")
+		return
+	}
+	var before int64
+	if raw := q.Get("before"); raw != "" {
+		before, err = strconv.ParseInt(raw, 10, 64)
+		if err != nil || before <= 0 {
+			writeError(w, 400, "invalid_cursor", "Refresh the conversation.")
+			return
+		}
+	}
+	result, err := s.Posts.Replies(r.Context(), s.Actor, repository, r.PathValue("id"), before)
+	if err != nil {
+		if errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostNotFound) || errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostVisibility) {
+			writeError(w, 404, "source_not_found", "Conversation is not visible.")
+		} else {
+			writeError(w, 503, "store_unavailable", "Could not read replies.")
+		}
+		return
+	}
+	if s.current(w, r) {
+		writeJSON(w, 200, result)
+	}
+}
+
+func (s Feed) retryPost(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+	var in struct {
+		CommandID        string `json:"command_id"`
+		Repository       string `json:"repository"`
+		ExpectedRevision *int64 `json:"expected_revision"`
+		Body             string `json:"body"`
+	}
+	if !decodeObject(w, r, &in) || !s.current(w, r) {
+		return
+	}
+	repository, err := strconv.ParseInt(in.Repository, 10, 64)
+	if err != nil || repository <= 0 || strconv.FormatInt(repository, 10) != in.Repository || in.ExpectedRevision == nil {
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Choose a canonical repository and expected revision.")
+		return
+	}
+	response, err := s.Commands.Retry(r.Context(), s.Actor, r.PathValue("id"), factory.FeedPostRetryRequest{CommandID: in.CommandID, Repository: repository, ExpectedRevision: *in.ExpectedRevision, Body: in.Body})
+	s.retryAnswer(w, r, response, err)
+}
+
+func (s Feed) retryReceipt(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
+	raw := r.URL.Query().Get("repository")
+	repository, err := strconv.ParseInt(raw, 10, 64)
+	if err != nil || repository <= 0 || strconv.FormatInt(repository, 10) != raw {
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Choose a canonical repository.")
+		return
+	}
+	response, err := s.Commands.RetryReceipt(r.Context(), s.Actor, r.PathValue("id"), r.PathValue("command"), repository)
+	s.retryAnswer(w, r, response, err)
+}
+
+func (s Feed) retryAnswer(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request, response factory.FeedPostRetryReceipt, err error) {
+	if err != nil {
+		switch {
+		case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostInputInvalid):
+			writeError(w, 400, "invalid_request", "Post retry scope or body is invalid.")
+		case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostNotFound), errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostVisibility):
+			writeError(w, 404, "comment_not_found", "Post not found.")
+		case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostAuthorRequired):
+			writeError(w, 403, "comment_author_required", "Only the author can revise this request.")
+		case errors.Is(err, factoryservice.ErrPostRetryConflict):
+			writeError(w, 409, "comment_retry_conflict", err.Error())
+		default:
+			writeError(w, 503, "store_unavailable", "Could not read the updated request.")
+		}
+		return
+	}
+	if s.current(w, r) {
+		writeJSON(w, 200, response)
+	}
+}
+
+// decodeObject decodes strict bounded JSON without host authentication.
+func decodeObject(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request, target any) bool {
+	err := strictjson.Decode(http.MaxBytesReader(w, r.Body, 65536), target)
+	if err == nil {
+		return true
+	}
+	var oversized *http.MaxBytesError
+	if errors.As(err, &oversized) {
+		writeError(w, 413, "body_too_large", "Request exceeds 64 KiB.")
+	} else {
+		writeError(w, 400, "invalid_json", "JSON fields or values are invalid.")
+	}
+	return false
+}
